<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
  <section xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-05-basic-interaction">
    <title>Basic Interaction</title>
    <introduction>
    <p>
        Now that the ship, lasso, and crystal all spawn, grow, and move together,
        let's create some basic interaction code. Since the prize interacts with
        both the collector and the ship, it is a good place to start for adding
        interaction effects. The initial effects will be the crystal disappearing
        on contact with the ship or collection by the lasso,
        energy/points for collecting with the lasso, and damage for the ship when
        colliding with the crystal.
    </p>
    </introduction>
    <subsection xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-basic-interaction-collecting-prizes">
      <title>Collecting Prizes</title>
      <p>
        The following changes are all to the prize script.
        First, create a signal for when the prize is
        collected with a value for the score/energy for collecting.
    </p>
    <program language="gdscript">
signal collected(value: int)
    </program>
    <p>
        Add a member variable that is an Array of the 
        lassos (Collector Nodes) that
        the prize is currently touching.
    </p>
    <program language="gdscript">
var _touching_collectors: Array[Node] = []
    </program>
     <p>
        At the end of <c>_process()</c> check to see
        if a collector is able to collect the prize.
      </p>
      <program language="gdscript">
func _process(delta: float) -> void:
    
    # ... code for changing sprite image 
    #     and prize value ...

    # call the collection interaction
    check_touching_collectors()
    </program>

    <p>
        The <c>check_touching_collectors</c> function loops 
        through the touching_collectors array and 
        checks if any of them are able to collect based 
        on the collection constraints. And if they are
        then the prize is removed from the scene and
        the collected energy is emitted.
    </p>
    <program language="gdscript">
func check_touching_collectors() -> void:
    for area in _touching_collectors:
        var collector: Collector = area as Collector
        if collector.can_collect(self.global_position):
            emit_signal("collected",value)
            queue_free()
    </program>
    <p>
        There are two companion functions that put the collectors
        into the touching_collectors array. These are _on_area_entered
        which uses the collisionarea2D's area entered signal,
    </p>
    <program language="gdscript">
func _on_area_entered(area: Area2D) -> void:
    if area.is_in_group("collector"):
        if area in _touching_collectors:
            return
        _touching_collectors.append(area)

    </program>
    <p>
        and _on_area_exited, which uses the CollisionArea2D's area_exited
        signal,
    </p>
    <program language="gdscript">
func _on_area_exited(area: Area2D) -> void:
    if area.is_in_group("collector"):
        if area in _touching_collectors:
            _touching_collectors.erase(area)
    </program>
      </subsection>
      <subsection xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-basic-interaction-health-impacts">
      <title>Health Impacts</title>
      <p>
        Create a signal for when the prize is hit by the 
        ship, and the amount of damage that the ship takes.
    </p>
    <program language="gdscript">
signal hit(value: int)
    </program>
      <p> 
        Since the ship is a RigidBody2D, the body_entered
        signal is used for when the ship makes contact with
        a prize and both destroys the prize and damages the ship
        using the hit signal.
    </p>
    <program language="gdscript">
func _on_body_entered(body: Node2D) -> void:
    if body.is_in_group("player"):
        emit_signal("hit",value)
        queue_free()
    </program>
      </subsection>
      <subsection xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-basic-interaction-playtesting">
      <title>Play Testing</title>
      <p>
        After adding the basic interaction, run the main scene and test if the 
        distance for collection looks good. Make sure that the crystal disappears
        both when the prize is collected and when the ship hits it.
        Make sure the ship is disabled after hitting the right amount 
        of crystals. Try changing values to see if game play improves.
        Think about which values increase or decrease difficulty so that 
        you can modify them as players get to higher levels.
      </p>
      </subsection>
    </section>
